-- ============================================================
-- Instinctive Fire: RAP coefficient
-- ============================================================

-- 0.12 = Arcane Shot's 0.15 ap_bonus x 0.8, per the design.
--
-- This is a SINGLE rank with a pure coefficient and no flat component, which is
-- an honest trade rather than a free win.  Arcane Shot's flat damage is roughly
-- 60% of its total at level 6 and ~35% at 79; a coefficient-only shot has none
-- of that, so Instinctive Fire is weak when first trained at 24 and converges to
-- about 80% of a coefficient-only Arcane Shot at 80.  It never delivers the
-- "60% of Arcane Shot's flat damage" half of the original design, because a
-- single rank has no per-rank flat value to be 60% of.
--
-- The alternative -- EffectRealPointsPerLevel1 with BaseLevel 24 / MaximumLevel
-- 80 -- does scale server-side (SpellInfo.cpp:411-428), but it is unverified
-- whether the 3.3.5a client applies RealPointsPerLevel when expanding $m1, so
-- the tooltip could lie at every level above 24.  Not adopted.
--
-- Because base points are 0, the description uses ${$RAP*0.12} and deliberately
-- has no +$m1 term: $m1 would render 1 (CalcValue = BasePoints + max(1, DieSides)).
DELETE FROM `spell_bonus_data` WHERE `entry` = 1462;
INSERT INTO `spell_bonus_data` (`entry`, `direct_bonus`, `dot_bonus`, `ap_bonus`, `ap_dot_bonus`, `comments`) VALUES
(1462, 0, 0, 0.12, 0, 'Hunter - Instinctive Fire (Arcane Shot 0.15 * 0.8)');

-- Notes on the columns that had to change and are easy to miss:
--   TargetCreatureType 1 -> 0   Beast Lore was beast-only; a damage shot is not.
--   AttributesEx        0x20400 -> 0x20000
--                               clears SPELL_ATTR1_NO_THREAT, which is correct
--                               for a lore-inspection spell and wrong for damage.
--   AttributesEx3       0x20000 -> 0
--                               clears SPELL_ATTR3_SUPPRESS_TARGET_PROCS
--                               ("no initial aggro").
--   SpellFamilyName     0 -> 9  required for SpellInfo::IsRangedWeaponSpell, and
--                               therefore for RAP rather than melee AP.
--   DamageClass         0 -> 3  ranged.
--   SchoolMask          8 -> 64 Arcane, matching Arcane Shot.  Physical would be
--                               routed through Unit::IsDamageReducedByArmor
--                               (Unit.cpp:2233) and armor would eat most of a
--                               pure-coefficient shot.
--   Category            0, RecoveryTime 8000
--                               its OWN cooldown.  Arcane Shot's Category 1173
--                               was rejected -- sharing it would put Arcane Shot
--                               on cooldown too.
--   SpellIconID         201 -> 5000
--                               Interface\Icons\INV_Ammo_Arrow_05.  That texture
--                               ships in enUS/patch-enUS.MPQ but has NO row in
--                               SpellIcon.dbc, so build_dbc.py adds one at id
--                               5000 (see CUSTOM_SPELL_ICONS there).  Spell.dbc's
--                               SpellIconID indexes SpellIcon.dbc -- 3.3.5a has
--                               no concept of the six-digit FileDataIDs modern
--                               tooling quotes, and its own ids stop at 4375.
--                               200742 carries the same icon so the buff-bar
--                               entry and the ability read as one thing.
--
-- The +20% ranged haste is a separate spell (200742) triggered on the caster by
-- Effect2, rather than an APPLY_AURA on 1462 itself, because the buff bar renders
-- SpellToolTip0: one spell cannot serve both the spellbook shot description and
-- the buff-bar haste text.

-- CastingTimeIndex 1 -> 18, for the same reason as Lacerating Shot: index 18 is
-- -1000000 ms, the "ranged special" marker shared by Arcane Shot, Serpent Sting
-- and Aimed Shot.  With index 1 and SPELL_ATTR0_USES_RANGED_SLOT set,
-- SpellInfo::CalcCastTime (SpellInfo.cpp:2758) adds 500 ms, giving an
-- unintended cast bar and the generic cast animation rather than a shot.
--
-- SpellVisual1 189 -> 3299 (Arcane Shot's): arrow missile model 1602 with
-- impact kit 419.  Beast Lore's own visual is a target-inspection effect with
-- no missile at all, so the shot had nothing to render in flight.
-- 200742 keeps CastingTimeIndex 1: it is a triggered self-buff, never cast, and
-- carries no USES_RANGED_SLOT bit for the +500 to apply to.

-- Auto Shot: ModalNextSpell 0 -> 75, spell 75 being Auto Shot.  This is what
-- starts auto-shot when a hunter fires a special, and it is why Instinctive
-- Fire did not.  Arcane Shot, Serpent Sting, Multi-Shot and Aimed Shot all set
-- it; none of them sets either INITIATE_COMBAT attribute.  See
-- woa_2026_08_11_02.sql for the full reasoning.
--
-- Also from the same 234-column diff against Arcane Shot (3044):
--   AttributesEx  131072 -> 0       drops SPELL_ATTR1_NO_AUTOCAST_AI, inherited
--                                   from Beast Lore and meaningless on a shot;
--                                   Arcane Shot has AttributesEx 0.
--   AttributesEx2 0 -> 131072       SPELL_ATTR2_DO_NOT_RESET_COMBAT_TIMERS, so
--                                   firing this does not clip the auto-shot
--                                   swing timer.
--   FacingCasterFlags 0 -> 1        must face the target.
-- 200742 sets none of these: it is a triggered self-buff, never cast at a target.
